      "title": "Assistant Men's and Women's Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Aurora University (IL) Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Men's and Women's Wrestling Coach | Aurora University (IL) Careers page has loaded. Assistant Men's and Women's Wrestling Coach | Aurora University (IL) Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Aurora University (IL) Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Men's and Women's Wrestling Coach Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Men's and Women's Wrestling Coach Salary $38,000.00 - $45,000.00 Annually Location Aurora, IL Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202500252 College/School Athletics Department Athletics Opening Date 09/01/2026 Description Benefits Questions Aurora University (AU) is committed to the transformative power of learning by creating a student-centered environment and an equity of experience and opportunity, to ensure that students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds feel welcome and included. Our culture of collaboration, generosity, and belonging make it a special place for students, faculty, and staff. AU is grounded in the transformative opportunity it provides to a diverse student body. As a private university with a public mission and a commitment to making a difference in peoples’ lives, AU has a long history of resilience and of providing access to an education that values innovation, focuses on continuous improvement, and has a positive impact on the communities we serve. We are proud of our service to and economic impact on the state of Illinois, where over 80% of our students stay to live and work, where 90% of our students come from, and where we foster strong community partnerships to develop the workforce in areas such as nursing, education, business, technology, and social work. We are looking for passionate and purposeful individuals who represent the full diversity of Aurora and who demonstrate a sensitivity to and understanding of the diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, ability, identity, and ethnic backgrounds present in our community. When you join the team at AU, you can expect to be part of an inclusive, innovative, and equity-focused community that approaches higher education as a matter of social justice requiring broad collaboration among faculty, staff, students, and community partners. At AU we believe that continuous learning is a fundamental part of working life, and our goal is for all colleagues on our campus to feel supported and equipped to realize their full potential. We actively support our community by providing all employees with opportunities to engage in professional development activities, as well as a range of tuition and employee benefits that can be found here . Position Purpose: The Assistant Men's and Women's Wrestling Coach supports the educational mission of Aurora University by assisting with the organization, administration, and day-to-day operation of the men's and women's wrestling programs. Working under the direction of the Director of Wrestling and/or Head Coach, this position contributes to student-athlete development, recruiting and retention, practice and competition preparation, program administration, and compliance with NCAA, conference, and institutional rules. Represents Aurora University in the most positive manner with prospective, former and current students, clients, suppliers and the community we serve. Interacts effectively with a diverse group of faculty, staff, students and other customers of our service, learns and uses operating practices of the department and Aurora University. Upholds the Mission Statement: Aurora University is an inclusive community dedicated to the transformative power of learning. As a teaching-centered institution, we encourage undergraduate and graduate students to discover what it takes to build meaningful and examined lives. Our singular goal is to empower our students to achieve lasting personal and professional success. Handles all information with tact and discretion and recognizes the confidential nature of university business. Supports learning through performance of essential job functions and performing other duties and functions as necessary or as assigned, including voluntary participation in university committees, activities and events. Essential Job Functions: Assists the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach with all aspects of the men's and women's wrestling programs, including coaching and instruction, recruiting and retention, practice and competition preparation, team travel, equipment, program administration, fundraising, and other duties assigned within the scope of the position. Collaborates effectively with the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach, assistant coaches, athletic training staff, strength and conditioning staff, athletics administrators, student workers, and other campus partners. Provides appropriate guidance to student managers or other assigned support personnel when directed. Understands and follows all NCAA, conference, and Aurora University rules, policies, and procedures, including NCAA recruiting legislation. Completes required compliance education and promptly reports any known or suspected violation to the appropriate athletics administrator. Teaching/Coaching Maintains current knowledge of collegiate wrestling rules, techniques, tactics, training methods, and sport-specific safety practices. Teaches wrestling skills and strategies consistent with the philosophy, standards, and competitive goals established by the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach. Assists in planning, conducting, and evaluating safe and effective practice sessions, individual skill instruction, strength and conditioning coordination, and competition preparation. Communicates expectations, praise, and corrective feedback clearly and constructively. Assists with scouting, match strategy, lineup and weight-management planning, film review, and the physical, mental, and emotional preparation of student-athletes for competition. Supports high expectations for academic achievement; monitors assigned student-athletes' academic progress and communicates concerns to the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach, and appropriate campus support services. Promotes student-athlete personal development, leadership, social responsibility, and engagement in university and community activities. Models and reinforces appropriate student-athlete conduct in and out of the athletic setting. Communicates behavioral concerns to the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach and supports established accountability procedures. Teaches and reinforces safe wrestling, training, weight-management, and facility practices. Monitors the condition of equipment and facilities and promptly reports safety concerns or maintenance needs to the appropriate staff member. Recruitment of Student-Athletes Actively recruits and assists in retaining qualified student-athletes for both the men's and women's wrestling programs. Helps execute the recruiting plan and works with the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach and Office of Admission to achieve approved roster and enrollment goals. Builds professional relationships with prospective student-athletes, families, coaches, and school personnel; evaluates prospects; conducts approved recruiting communications and visits; maintains accurate recruiting records; and explains Aurora University's academic, athletic, and NCAA Division III opportunities. Assists with the selection, inventory, distribution, collection, care, and maintenance of uniforms, wrestling equipment, and program supplies in accordance with the approved budget and purchasing procedures. Completes assigned administrative responsibilities accurately and on time, which may include recruiting records, travel itineraries, expense documentation, compliance forms, eligibility and roster information, competition entries, end-of-season materials, and program reports. Assists with maintaining team and individual records, statistics, video, and historical information, and works with Sports Information staff to provide accurate and timely program information. Maintains self-control and poise and models sportsmanship and professional conduct in interactions with student-athletes, officials, opponents, spectators, colleagues, and community members. Assists with alumni engagement, fundraising, camps and clinics, community service, and other activities that support the visibility and advancement of Aurora University wrestling, as assigned and in accordance with institutional policy. Attends and participates in athletics department meetings, staff meetings, compliance education, professional development, university functions, and program activities as required. Supports both the men's and women's wrestling programs and carries out responsibilities assigned by the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach. Works collaboratively across both programs while respecting established reporting lines and coaching responsibilities. Handles student, recruiting, personnel, medical, academic, and university information with tact, discretion, and appropriate confidentiality. Drives university or rental vehicles, when authorized, and assists with team travel supervision, transportation, lodging, meals, itineraries, and student-athlete accountability for away competitions and other program activities. Performs special and/or additional duties consistent with the position as assigned by the Director of Wrestling/Head Coach or Vice President for Athletics. Assists in fostering an inclusive, respectful, disciplined, and student-centered team culture that supports the success and well-being of men's and women's wrestling student-athletes. Essential Job Requirements: Education: Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree preferred. Experience: Minimum of 1–2 years of coaching experience required. Collegiate wrestling experience preferred, with prior collegiate coaching and recruiting experience strongly preferred. Skills: Strong organizational and time-management skills, with working knowledge of NCAA Division III compliance standards and recruiting regulations. Demonstrated ability to teach wrestling technique, plan training activities, and contribute effectively within a collaborative coaching staff. Excellent verbal, written, and electronic communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with student-athletes, prospective students, families, coaches, officials, alumni, administrators, support staff, and the campus and local communities. Ability to work independently within assigned responsibilities, follow the program's established direction, meet deadlines, solve problems, and communicate proactively. Proficiency with common office, recruiting, communication, video, and athletics-management technology. Strong knowledge of collegiate wrestling and a demonstrated commitment to student-athlete development, academic success, sportsmanship, inclusion, and well-being. Physical Requirements: Ability to communicate effectively in person, by telephone, and through written and electronic media. Ability to move throughout campus, wrestling facilities, competition venues, and recruiting locations; demonstrate and instruct wrestling techniques; and lift, move, or transport equipment and supplies as needed, with or without reasonable accommodation. Regular evening, early-morning, weekend, and holiday availability is required during portions of the academic and competitive year. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced and evolving intercollegiate athletics environment. Work Hours: This is a full-time (40 hours), on-campus position. Work hours vary based on practices, competitions, recruiting, travel, meetings, camps, and other program responsibilities and will regularly include evenings and weekends. Special Requirements: A valid driver's license and driving record that meet institutional requirements are required. Regular travel is required for competitions, recruiting, meetings, and other program activities, including travel between campus and athletics locations. The pay range referenced in the job posting is the budgeted amount the university reasonably expects to pay for this position. The final pay rate will not be below the lowest pay rate listed herein. Benefit-eligible positions offer excellent benefits including health, dental, life, vision, long term disability, a 403(b) retirement plan through TIAA, and tuition remission. Aurora University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Aurora University offers competitive, flexible benefits to eligible employees. Health Insurance Choice of HMO or PPO offered through BlueCross BlueShield of Illinois. Dental and Vision Insurance Choice of two dental plans and vision insurance offered through Blue Cross Blue Shield. Life Insurance and AD&D 1.5 times annual salary, dependent on age. Additional life insurance also may be purchased for self, spouse, and children. Long Term Disability 60% of salary, taxable and nontaxable options. TIAA Retirement Account The University offers a 403b retirement plan, administered by TIAA. Matching contributions offered first day of employment to eligible employees, at the discretion of the University and Board of Directors. Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) FSAs are available for medical costs and dependent care costs. Paid Time Off Vacation, personal, and sick leave are provided to eligible employees. Holidays The university observes nine major holidays where the university is closed. Tuition Assistance Tuition assistance for AU undergraduate courses is available to eligible employees and eligible family members beginning the term following one (1) year of regular, full-time employment. Tuition assistance for graduate programs paid at 60% for employee following Senior Leadership approval. Tuition Exchange Consortiums AU is a member of the Tuition Exchange (TE) and the Council of Independent Colleges Tuition Exchange Program (CIC-TEP) enabling full-time employees and eligible family members to be eligible for tuition assistance at more than 600 universities nationwide. Eligibility for the CIC-TEP and TE programs is one (1) year of regular, full-time employment as of 8/31. To see more benefits details and breakdowns please see our benefits guide here . 01 Which statement below best describes the highest level of education you have completed? High school graduate, diploma or the equivalent (GED) Associate degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Professional degree Doctorate degree Doctor of Philosophy 02 How many years of coaching experience do you have? No experience Less than 1 year of experience 1 year but less than 2 years of experience 2 years but less than 3 years experience 3 or more years of experience 03 Do you have collegiate wrestling experience? Yes No 04 Do you have prior collegiate coaching and recruiting experience? Yes No Required Question Employer Aurora University (IL) Address 347 S. Gladstone Ave. Aurora, Illinois, 60506 Phone 630-844-5493 Website www.aurora.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Aurora University (IL) Careers Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu Aurora University (IL) Careers Job Opportunities Transfer Jobs Email Job Alerts Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Facebook LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com, Schooljobs.com, and our mobile app(s) (collectively referred to